  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A Quiet Place-Setting Ritual",
    "overview": "A shared meal is the visual world: softly painted food, a warm steaming pot, recognizable fictional friends and one empty chair. Pastel gouache and airbrush textures provide fine grain, softly imperfect edges and natural volume. Generous near-white space and quiet Instrument Sans leave the illustrations room to breathe. Controls appear beside the object they change.\n\nThe user's NONO MARKET direction governs material, whitespace and typographic restraint. The artwork is cohesive illustration: food already sits on painted porcelain, portraits have individual faces and the pot has warm volume. The interface uses Tomato for commitment and Leaf for dietary, protected and suggested states. It retains the directly editable table experiment and its separate, explicit recommendation preview.",
